    {
      "@id": "skills/kg/kg-core/instance-publication.md#provenance-1",
      "@type": "prov:Entity",
      "cat-harness:provenanceKind": "bean",
      "cat-harness:section": "instance-publication — draft is a state, not an absence of one",
      "prov:value": "> Skill id: `instance-publication` · Package: `folio-core` · Instance:\n> `cat-harness` · Bean `9wb0`",
      "cat-harness:refs": [
        "bean 9wb0"
      ]
    },
    {
      "@id": "skills/kg/kg-core/instance-publication.md#provenance-2",
      "@type": "prov:Entity",
      "cat-harness:provenanceKind": "owner-decision",
      "cat-harness:section": "instance-publication — draft is a state, not an absence of one",
      "prov:value": "The owner, 2026-09-23:\n\n> all assets get a version and are in \"draft\" publication. formal publication\n> process needs to be deinfed/neeeds tools/depends on instance",
      "cat-harness:refs": [
        "2026-09-23"
      ],
      "dcterms:date": [
        "2026-09-23"
      ]
    },
    {
      "@id": "skills/kg/kg-core/instance-publication.md#provenance-3",
      "@type": "prov:Entity",
      "cat-harness:provenanceKind": "history",
      "cat-harness:section": "1. Every asset carries a `version` — and the `id` is HELD",
      "prov:value": "**It is enforced by `check:publishable`, not by the schema**, and that is a\nmeasured decision rather than a weaker one: requiring it in the type breaks\n**376 tests across 20+ files**, every fixture that builds a declaration\nwithout it."
    },
    {
      "@id": "skills/kg/kg-core/instance-publication.md#provenance-4",
      "@type": "prov:Entity",
      "cat-harness:provenanceKind": "history",
      "cat-harness:section": "1. Every asset carries a `version` — and the `id` is HELD",
      "prov:value": "**`id` is a different story, and it is not shipped.** The owner ruled the\nnamespace `io.github.litlfred.folio-assistant.<name>`; it was minted into all\n17 declarations and then **removed**, because the next ruling contradicts\nwriting it there at all:\n\n> i want simplest so if someone wants to bootstrap a different harness, there\n> is only one place to change. **ONE PLACE.**\n>\n> fork would only edit `bootstrap/README.md` and change ONE reference there."
    },
    {
      "@id": "skills/kg/kg-core/instance-publication.md#provenance-5",
      "@type": "prov:Entity",
      "cat-harness:provenanceKind": "bean",
      "cat-harness:section": "1. Every asset carries a `version` — and the `id` is HELD",
      "prov:value": "`bootstrap/README.md` today carries **zero** outward references and its own\ntests enforce that. Bean `iwtn` owns creating it.",
      "cat-harness:refs": [
        "bean iwtn"
      ]
    },
    {
      "@id": "skills/kg/kg-core/instance-publication.md#provenance-6",
      "@type": "prov:Entity",
      "cat-harness:provenanceKind": "history",
      "cat-harness:section": "1. Every asset carries a `version` — and the `id` is HELD",
      "prov:value": "This reverses what `instance-versioning.md` §3.1 originally shipped, which\n**refused** them unless an instance declared `publishable: true`:\n\n> refused while `publishable` is undeclared — a declared `version` reads as a\n> published identity, and nobody has said this instance is published"
    },
    {
      "@id": "skills/kg/kg-core/instance-publication.md#provenance-7",
      "@type": "prov:Entity",
      "cat-harness:provenanceKind": "history",
      "cat-harness:section": "2. Publication is a STATE, and the state is `draft`",
      "prov:value": "**This is why the old model reported a fully-decided corpus as a worklist.**"
    },
    {
      "@id": "skills/kg/kg-core/instance-publication.md#provenance-8",
      "@type": "prov:Entity",
      "cat-harness:provenanceKind": "history",
      "cat-harness:section": "3. `published` is REFUSED by the schema, not merely reported",
      "prov:value": "A flag nothing can verify is precisely the ceremony §3.1 was written against."
    },
    {
      "@id": "skills/kg/kg-core/instance-publication.md#provenance-9",
      "@type": "prov:Entity",
      "cat-harness:provenanceKind": "owner-decision",
      "cat-harness:section": "The id namespace — one rule, no per-instance invention",
      "prov:value": "Owner's ruling, 2026-09-23: **`io.github.litlfred.folio-assistant.<name>` for\nall 17.**",
      "cat-harness:refs": [
        "2026-09-23"
      ],
      "dcterms:date": [
        "2026-09-23"
      ]
    },
    {
      "@id": "skills/kg/kg-core/instance-publication.md#provenance-10",
      "@type": "prov:Entity",
      "cat-harness:provenanceKind": "history",
      "cat-harness:section": "A MIRROR NEVER TAKES ITS SUBJECT'S IDENTITY",
      "prov:value": "**The same reading governs `canonicalUrl`,** and the DAK layer's own declaration\nalready said so before this skill existed."
    },
    {
      "@id": "skills/kg/kg-core/instance-publication.md#provenance-11",
      "@type": "prov:Entity",
      "cat-harness:provenanceKind": "owner-decision",
      "cat-harness:section": "Three questions that must not be merged — publication, staging, mirroring",
      "prov:value": "Owner, 2026-10-05: *\"there is staging vs publication being conflated here.\"*",
      "cat-harness:refs": [
        "2026-10-05"
      ],
      "dcterms:date": [
        "2026-10-05"
      ]
    },
    {
      "@id": "skills/kg/kg-core/instance-publication.md#provenance-12",
      "@type": "prov:Entity",
      "cat-harness:provenanceKind": "owner-decision",
      "cat-harness:section": "Release IRIs — one address, the major, derived from the version",
      "prov:value": "**Owner, 2026-10-23 (option \"B. Major in address\"):** every address an\ninstance mints carries its **major version only** — `<iriBase>v<major>/…` —\nwhoever reads it.",
      "cat-harness:refs": [
        "2026-10-23"
      ],
      "dcterms:date": [
        "2026-10-23"
      ]
    },
    {
      "@id": "skills/kg/kg-core/instance-publication.md#provenance-13",
      "@type": "prov:Entity",
      "cat-harness:provenanceKind": "history",
      "cat-harness:section": "Release IRIs — one address, the major, derived from the version",
      "prov:value": "Why it changed: until this ruling (owner, 2026-09-29) a program-read address\ncarried the full semver, `…/bootstrap/0.1.0/ns#`, on the reasoning that a\nprogram pins exactly.",
      "cat-harness:refs": [
        "2026-09-29"
      ],
      "dcterms:date": [
        "2026-09-29"
      ]
    },
    {
      "@id": "skills/kg/kg-core/instance-publication.md#provenance-14",
      "@type": "prov:Entity",
      "cat-harness:provenanceKind": "bean",
      "cat-harness:section": "Release IRIs — one address, the major, derived from the version",
      "prov:value": "Moving the base itself — a fork, or\nbootstrap's move off `litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/bootstrap/` (bean\n`r3gy`, group E) — is `bun run iri:sync -- --from <old base>`, once. `beans/`\nis never rewritten: a bean records what was true when it was written."
    },
    {
      "@id": "skills/kg/kg-core/instance-publication.md#provenance-15",
      "@type": "prov:Entity",
      "cat-harness:provenanceKind": "proposal",
      "cat-harness:section": "Release IRIs — one address, the major, derived from the version",
      "prov:value": "Until\nevery litlfred layer carries `<iriBase>v<major>/` (bootstrap-tools#39 lists\nthose that do not, with counts; added 2026-10-23), the CHECKS —\n`check:node-iris`, `iri:sync:check`, `vocabulary:check` — accept a legacy\n`<iriBase><semver>/` copy whose MAJOR is the declared major as\n**deprecated**: a warning naming the file, not a failure.",
      "cat-harness:refs": [
        "#39",
        "2026-10-23"
      ],
      "dcterms:date": [
        "2026-10-23"
      ]
    },
    {
      "@id": "skills/kg/kg-core/instance-publication.md#provenance-16",
      "@type": "prov:Entity",
      "cat-harness:provenanceKind": "bean",
      "cat-harness:section": "Release IRIs — one address, the major, derived from the version",
      "prov:value": "`kg-export` mints it from where the document is actually\nserved, and today that is this site; pointing it at a base that serves nothing\nis the failure `40fl` / #718 recorded. It moves when the bootstrap repository\npublishes.",
      "cat-harness:refs": [
        "#718"
      ]
    },
    {
      "@id": "skills/kg/kg-core/instance-publication.md#provenance-17",
      "@type": "prov:Entity",
      "cat-harness:provenanceKind": "history",
      "cat-harness:section": "The release site — what is served where",
      "prov:value": "The IRI rule above says what an identifier IS; this says what the instance's\nown site must serve so that every identifier dereferences. Written 2026-09-29\nfor the bootstrap split, after the separation analysis found every bootstrap\nidentifier pointing at an address nothing yet served.",
      "cat-harness:refs": [
        "2026-09-29"
      ],
      "dcterms:date": [
        "2026-09-29"
      ]
    },
    {
      "@id": "skills/kg/kg-core/instance-publication.md#provenance-18",
      "@type": "prov:Entity",
      "cat-harness:provenanceKind": "history",
      "cat-harness:section": "The release site — what is served where",
      "prov:value": "Since the 2026-10-23 ruling one directory serves both audiences, as one\naddress does.",
      "cat-harness:refs": [
        "2026-10-23"
      ],
      "dcterms:date": [
        "2026-10-23"
      ]
    },
    {
      "@id": "skills/kg/kg-core/instance-publication.md#provenance-19",
      "@type": "prov:Entity",
      "cat-harness:provenanceKind": "history",
      "cat-harness:section": "The release site — what is served where",
      "prov:value": "`check:node-iris` enforces it; the two\n  discussion schemas failed it until 2026-09-29.",
      "cat-harness:refs": [
        "2026-09-29"
      ],
      "dcterms:date": [
        "2026-09-29"
      ]
    },
    {
      "@id": "skills/kg/kg-core/instance-publication.md#provenance-20",
      "@type": "prov:Entity",
      "cat-harness:provenanceKind": "bean",
      "cat-harness:section": "The release site — what is served where",
      "prov:value": "- **An instance's own site serves only what its tools generate** (owner,\n  2026-09-30, Q3 of bean `xsqm`).",
      "cat-harness:refs": [
        "bean xsqm",
        "2026-09-30"
      ],
      "dcterms:date": [
        "2026-09-30"
      ]
    },
    {
      "@id": "skills/kg/kg-core/instance-publication.md#provenance-21",
      "@type": "prov:Entity",
      "cat-harness:provenanceKind": "bean",
      "cat-harness:section": "The JSON-LD context: `<iriBase>ns/context/v1.jsonld`, published by the instance",
      "prov:value": "It is\n`@protected`, so a change that rebinds a term is a new `v2` beside it, never an\nedit under a cached URL. **Owner, 2026-10-15** (bean `folio-assistant-63q4`):\neach repository publishes its own context, through ONE reusable workflow, and\n**the initiation process sets that up**.",
      "cat-harness:refs": [
        "bean folio-assistant-63q4",
        "2026-10-15"
      ],
      "dcterms:date": [
        "2026-10-15"
      ]
    },
    {
      "@id": "skills/kg/kg-core/instance-publication.md#provenance-22",
      "@type": "prov:Entity",
      "cat-harness:provenanceKind": "owner-decision",
      "cat-harness:section": "The JSON-LD context: `<iriBase>ns/context/v1.jsonld`, published by the instance",
      "prov:value": "**Where its `ns` is a document, the context goes beside it.** Owner,\n2026-10-15 (\"D1\"): an instance holding its vocabulary as `ns.jsonld` at its\nroot (bootstrap) has `ns` staged as a FILE (the extensionless `ns`, and\n`v<major>/ns`), so `ns/` cannot also be the directory `ns/context/v1.jsonld`\nneeds, and a static host cannot serve both.",
      "cat-harness:refs": [
        "2026-10-15"
      ],
      "dcterms:date": [
        "2026-10-15"
      ]
    },
    {
      "@id": "skills/kg/kg-core/instance-publication.md#provenance-23",
      "@type": "prov:Entity",
      "cat-harness:provenanceKind": "owner-decision",
      "cat-harness:section": "Tags",
      "prov:value": "A standalone repository — one instance, declared at its root — tags a release\nplainly, `v<major>.<minor>.<patch>`; a repository of several instances tags\n`<name>-v<major>.<minor>.<patch>`, because a plain tag could not say which\ninstance it released (owner, 2026-09-30). `check:version-bump` reads both\naccordingly.",
      "cat-harness:refs": [
        "2026-09-30"
      ],
      "dcterms:date": [
        "2026-09-30"
      ]
    },
    {
      "@id": "skills/kg/kg-core/instance-publication.md#provenance-24",
      "@type": "prov:Entity",
      "cat-harness:provenanceKind": "owner-decision",
      "cat-harness:section": "What each instance publishes — graph, address, schema, and what is stripped",
      "prov:value": "Owner, 2026-10-02, opening bean `4ak5`: *\"there are some rules in the KG\ncorpsu but scattered.\"*",
      "cat-harness:refs": [
        "bean 4ak5",
        "2026-10-02"
      ],
      "dcterms:date": [
        "2026-10-02"
      ]
    },
    {
      "@id": "skills/kg/kg-core/instance-publication.md#provenance-25",
      "@type": "prov:Entity",
      "cat-harness:provenanceKind": "bean",
      "cat-harness:section": "One document per declared instance, of its own directories",
      "prov:value": "The set is read from the declarations\n(`instanceRootsIn`), never listed in a workflow: a list went stale the way\nsuch lists do, missing every instance added since `l4ay`."
    },
    {
      "@id": "skills/kg/kg-core/instance-publication.md#provenance-26",
      "@type": "prov:Entity",
      "cat-harness:provenanceKind": "bean",
      "cat-harness:section": "One document per declared instance, of its own directories",
      "prov:value": "| the checkout root, `folio-assistant` | `<site>/<stub>/<stub>.jsonld` | `kg-export.ts --instance .` (bean `l4ay`) |",
      "cat-harness:refs": [
        "bean l4ay"
      ]
    },
    {
      "@id": "skills/kg/kg-core/instance-publication.md#provenance-27",
      "@type": "prov:Entity",
      "cat-harness:provenanceKind": "proposal",
      "cat-harness:section": "One document per declared instance, of its own directories",
      "prov:value": "- **The host is in the same place as every other layer.** Its document sat\n  at the site root, `<site>/<stub>.jsonld`, until the owner's ruling of\n  2026-10-23 (decision 1b on\n  [cat-harness-tools#603](https://github.com/litlfred/cat-harness-tools/issues/603)):\n  *the host is no longer special*.",
      "cat-harness:refs": [
        "#603",
        "2026-10-23"
      ],
      "dcterms:date": [
        "2026-10-23"
      ]
    },
    {
      "@id": "skills/kg/kg-core/instance-publication.md#provenance-28",
      "@type": "prov:Entity",
      "cat-harness:provenanceKind": "proposal",
      "cat-harness:section": "One document per declared instance, of its own directories",
      "prov:value": "- **The host is built in instance scope** since #2135 (owner ruling\n  2026-10-05, option B; bean `4ak5` item 2).",
      "cat-harness:refs": [
        "bean 4ak5",
        "#2135",
        "2026-10-05"
      ],
      "dcterms:date": [
        "2026-10-05"
      ]
    },
    {
      "@id": "skills/kg/kg-core/instance-publication.md#provenance-29",
      "@type": "prov:Entity",
      "cat-harness:provenanceKind": "proposal",
      "cat-harness:section": "An `@id` that moved is not forwarded",
      "prov:value": "A clean break (owner, 2026-11-02,\n[litlfred/cat-harness-tools#1378](https://github.com/litlfred/cat-harness-tools/issues/1378);\nit closed #962).",
      "cat-harness:refs": [
        "litlfred/cat-harness-tools#1378",
        "#962",
        "2026-11-02"
      ],
      "dcterms:date": [
        "2026-11-02"
      ]
    },
    {
      "@id": "skills/kg/kg-core/instance-publication.md#provenance-30",
      "@type": "prov:Entity",
      "cat-harness:provenanceKind": "bean",
      "cat-harness:section": "Which base an `@id` is minted against",
      "prov:value": "With no base at all the `@id` is\ndocument-relative and a problem is reported, never a guessed absolute one\n(bean `40fl`). **Every instance this site publishes, the host included,\nsits at `<base>/<name>/<stub>.jsonld`** (bean `dyd3`; the host since the\nowner's ruling of 2026-10-23, decision 1b on\n[cat-harness-tools#603](https://github.com/litlfred/cat-harness-tools/issues/603):\none rule for every layer, with subjects beside their document).",
      "cat-harness:refs": [
        "bean 40fl",
        "bean dyd3",
        "#603",
        "2026-10-23"
      ],
      "dcterms:date": [
        "2026-10-23"
      ]
    },
    {
      "@id": "skills/kg/kg-core/instance-publication.md#provenance-31",
      "@type": "prov:Entity",
      "cat-harness:provenanceKind": "proposal",
      "cat-harness:section": "Which base an `@id` is minted against",
      "prov:value": "Today it is the host of its own\nbase, so its `@id` is `<canonicalUrl>/<stub>.jsonld` (#1548). Where its\ndocument and subjects go under the one rule is phase 2 of #603,\n[cat-harness-tools#638](https://github.com/litlfred/cat-harness-tools/issues/638).",
      "cat-harness:refs": [
        "#1548",
        "#603",
        "#638"
      ]
    },
    {
      "@id": "skills/kg/kg-core/instance-publication.md#provenance-32",
      "@type": "prov:Entity",
      "cat-harness:provenanceKind": "history",
      "cat-harness:section": "Which base an `@id` is minted against",
      "prov:value": "**What goes after the base** is a path, not a `#fragment`: a subject is\n`<doc dir>/<kind>/<id>` (owner, 2026-10-23), served as its own file. The rule, its reasons,\nthe `ns#Term` exception and the migration of today's `….jsonld#…` IRIs are in\n[`kg-export`](kg-export.md) §\"Subject IRIs — a path, not a `#fragment`\".",
      "cat-harness:refs": [
        "2026-10-23"
      ],
      "dcterms:date": [
        "2026-10-23"
      ]
    },
    {
      "@id": "skills/kg/kg-core/instance-publication.md#provenance-33",
      "@type": "prov:Entity",
      "cat-harness:provenanceKind": "proposal",
      "cat-harness:section": "The schema",
      "prov:value": "They sit under the host's own directory, beside its\ndocument, like everything else it publishes ([litlfred/cat-harness-tools#676](https://github.com/litlfred/cat-harness-tools/issues/676),",
      "cat-harness:refs": [
        "litlfred/cat-harness-tools#676"
      ]
    },
    {
      "@id": "skills/kg/kg-core/instance-publication.md#provenance-34",
      "@type": "prov:Entity",
      "cat-harness:provenanceKind": "bean",
      "cat-harness:section": "603 decision 1b(i)). Each old site-root address holds a tombstone for one",
      "prov:value": "**Every instance `instance-exports.ts` publishes also publishes\n`<site>/<stub>/schema/`** (owner ruling 2026-10-05, option B; bean `4ak5`\nitem 1).",
      "cat-harness:refs": [
        "bean 4ak5",
        "2026-10-05"
      ],
      "dcterms:date": [
        "2026-10-05"
      ]
    },
    {
      "@id": "skills/kg/kg-core/instance-publication.md#provenance-35",
      "@type": "prov:Entity",
      "cat-harness:provenanceKind": "bean",
      "cat-harness:section": "603 decision 1b(i)). Each old site-root address holds a tombstone for one",
      "prov:value": "**The host links its own\n`<stub>.schema.json`**, the shared declaration schema, by the `$id`\n`buildDeclarationSchema` mints with the same base (bean `4ak5` follow-up,\nowner-approved 2026-10-05).",
      "cat-harness:refs": [
        "bean 4ak5",
        "2026-10-05"
      ],
      "dcterms:date": [
        "2026-10-05"
      ]
    },
    {
      "@id": "skills/kg/kg-core/instance-publication.md#provenance-36",
      "@type": "prov:Entity",
      "cat-harness:provenanceKind": "history",
      "cat-harness:section": "603 decision 1b(i)). Each old site-root address holds a tombstone for one",
      "prov:value": "That holds in the instance's own document and in a\ncheckout-scope build that stacks it. Before the follow-up those edges were\nleft unset, and `hasIOContract` read `false`."
    },
    {
      "@id": "skills/kg/kg-core/instance-publication.md#provenance-37",
      "@type": "prov:Entity",
      "cat-harness:provenanceKind": "owner-decision",
      "cat-harness:section": "Which Zod schemas are public",
      "prov:value": "**Owner ruling 2026-10-05, option C: \"every exported \\*Schema\".** In the\nowner's words: *\"Render all exported Zod \\*Schema consts per instance now; may\nexpose internal schemas.\"*",
      "cat-harness:refs": [
        "2026-10-05"
      ],
      "dcterms:date": [
        "2026-10-05"
      ]
    },
    {
      "@id": "skills/kg/kg-core/instance-publication.md#provenance-38",
      "@type": "prov:Entity",
      "cat-harness:provenanceKind": "owner-decision",
      "cat-harness:section": "Which Zod schemas are public",
      "prov:value": "Publishing a schema says it is reachable,\nnot that it is stable: the owner accepted that internal schemas are exposed."
    },
    {
      "@id": "skills/kg/kg-core/instance-publication.md#provenance-39",
      "@type": "prov:Entity",
      "cat-harness:provenanceKind": "bean",
      "cat-harness:section": "Which Zod schemas are public",
      "prov:value": "**The JSON-LD document drops `schemas` from its own `omitted` once it links\nthe index** (bean `4ak5` follow-up, owner-approved 2026-10-05). Its module-level\n`Schema` collector is still instance-bound and does not run for a foreign\ninstance.",
      "cat-harness:refs": [
        "bean 4ak5",
        "2026-10-05"
      ],
      "dcterms:date": [
        "2026-10-05"
      ]
    },
    {
      "@id": "skills/kg/kg-core/instance-publication.md#provenance-40",
      "@type": "prov:Entity",
      "cat-harness:provenanceKind": "history",
      "cat-harness:section": "Which Zod schemas are public",
      "prov:value": "The publisher imports each module and reads\nevery key, so `export { FooSchema } from \"./x\"` and `export { X as YSchema }`\nwere always rendered. The gate's text half now reads them as well\n(`declaredExportNames`): `export const`, `export { … }` lists with or without\n`from`, the name after `as`, and `export * as N`."
    },
    {
      "@id": "skills/kg/kg-core/instance-publication.md#provenance-41",
      "@type": "prov:Entity",
      "cat-harness:provenanceKind": "bean",
      "cat-harness:section": "Named subgraphs, and the root index above them",
      "prov:value": "- **Named subgraphs** (bean `c1m4`): `<site>/subgraph/<HARNESS>/<PATH>/`, with\n  `index.jsonld` (direct members as pointers) and `index.hydrated.jsonld`\n  (every member inline, deep).",
      "cat-harness:refs": [
        "bean c1m4"
      ]
    },
    {
      "@id": "skills/kg/kg-core/instance-publication.md#provenance-42",
      "@type": "prov:Entity",
      "cat-harness:provenanceKind": "owner-decision",
      "cat-harness:section": "Named subgraphs, and the root index above them",
      "prov:value": "- **The root index** (item 3): `<site>/index.jsonld` and `index.json`, built\n  at publish time by `root-index.ts` and never committed (owner,\n  2026-10-04): a committed copy conflicts whenever two PRs change the set of\n  harnesses.",
      "cat-harness:refs": [
        "2026-10-04"
      ],
      "dcterms:date": [
        "2026-10-04"
      ]
    },
    {
      "@id": "skills/kg/kg-core/instance-publication.md#provenance-43",
      "@type": "prov:Entity",
      "cat-harness:provenanceKind": "owner-decision",
      "cat-harness:section": "What is never in a published graph",
      "prov:value": "- **`fsh-guts`.** Owner, 2026-09-19: *\"NEVER include fsh-guts, references to\n  fsh-guts stripped out of KG before sending to publication.\"*",
      "cat-harness:refs": [
        "2026-09-19"
      ],
      "dcterms:date": [
        "2026-09-19"
      ]
    },
    {
      "@id": "skills/kg/kg-core/instance-publication.md#provenance-44",
      "@type": "prov:Entity",
      "cat-harness:provenanceKind": "history",
      "cat-harness:section": "What is never in a published graph",
      "prov:value": "No collector in `kg-export.ts` reads a state\n  graph's files (measured 2026-10-05). Where such contents are published, it\n  is as their declared Subgraph node's own document (`todos.jsonld`,\n  [`directory-conventions`](directory-conventions.md) §\"Publishing a\n  subgraph's contents\"), as a SQLite slice built at deploy (bean `q8ar`), or\n  on a branch rather than the site (QA verdicts, on `qa-reports`).",
      "cat-harness:refs": [
        "bean q8ar",
        "2026-10-05"
      ],
      "dcterms:date": [
        "2026-10-05"
      ]
    },
    {
      "@id": "skills/kg/kg-core/instance-publication.md#provenance-45",
      "@type": "prov:Entity",
      "cat-harness:provenanceKind": "history",
      "cat-harness:section": "Do not",
      "prov:value": "Inferring from them is how a boolean\n  defaulting to `false` erases the difference between \"decided\" and \"nobody\n  looked\" — the defect §3.1 was right about even where its model was wrong."
    },
    {
      "@id": "skills/kg/kg-core/instance-publication.md#provenance-46",
      "@type": "prov:Entity",
      "cat-harness:provenanceKind": "bean",
      "cat-harness:section": "Do not",
      "prov:value": "- **Do not restate this skill in a bean, a proposal or `AGENTS.md`.** `kn0t`\n  restated `ig-publisher-reduction` and drifted from it in four places within a\n  day, one of which would have let a phase be approved on an impression."
    },
    {
      "@id": "skills/kg/kg-core/instance-publication.md#provenance-47",
      "@type": "prov:Entity",
      "cat-harness:provenanceKind": "bean",
      "cat-harness:section": "Named subgraphs, and the root index above them",
      "prov:value": "- **Named subgraphs** (bean `c1m4`): `<site>/subgraph/<HARNESS>/<PATH>/`, with\n  `index.jsonld` (direct members as pointers) and `index.hydrated.jsonld`\n  (every member inline, deep). **The harness root has `index.jsonld` only**,\n  because a deep hydrated file there is the monolith `f233` forbids.\n  `gen-subgraph-jsonld.ts` frames each instance from its OWN export, so no\n  subgraph names a `cat-harness.jsonld#<foreign>` fragment. The tree is\n  committed under `cat-harness/docs/subgraph/`, its `@context` is\n  `<site>/ns/subgraph/v1.jsonld`, and heavy bodies are content-addressed\n  payloads under `cat-harness/docs/payload/sha256/`, copied verbatim to\n  `<site>/payload/`. `bootstrap` and `bootstrap-tools` publish their own\n  subgraphs, and the repository index links them with `rdfs:seeAlso`\n  (bean `t8c4`). The contract: [`kg-export`](kg-export.md) §\"Named\n  subgraphs\" and §\"Payloads\".\n- **The root index** (item 3): `<site>/index.jsonld` and `index.json`, built\n  at publish time by `root-index.ts` and never committed (owner,\n  2026-10-04): a committed copy conflicts whenever two PRs change the set of\n  harnesses. It names every declared instance at depth 1, with no node of\n  any graph inlined. It exits 1, having written nothing, when an instance's\n  export is not where its identity says, rather than publish a shorter map.",
      "cat-harness:refs": [
        "bean t8c4"
      ],
      "dcterms:date": [
        "2026-10-04"
      ]
    }
  ]
}
